00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:30.210
Yes.
没错。

309
00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:40.110
The first recorded duel in America took place in 1621 in the Massachusetts Bay Colony.
美国第一次有记载的决斗发生在1621年的马萨诸塞湾殖民地。

310
00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:46.190
And then America created their own set of dueling rules.
后来美国制定了自己的一套决斗规则。

311
00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:47.230
Oh.
噢。

312
00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:52.990
They were written by South Carolina Governor John Wilson in 1838.
它们是由南卡罗来纳州州长约翰·威尔逊在1838年编写的。

313
00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:59.230
So, in a typical American duel, each party has to act through a second.
所以，在典型的美国式决斗中，双方都必须通过代理人进行。

314
00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:02.930
I know this from the musical Hamilton, everyone.
我是从音乐剧《汉密尔顿》里知道的，各位。

315
00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:03.990
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

316
00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:06.490
Oh, like you have your partner that goes with you.
噢，就像你带个搭档一起去那样。

317
00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:07.050
Yes.
是的。

318
00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.010
Like your buddy.
就像你的好哥们。

319
00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:08.790
That's right.
没错。

320
00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:09.550
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

321
00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.390
And don't you get to bring like a medic?
难道不能带个医护人员吗？

322
00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:12.350
Like a doctor?
比如医生？

323
00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:13.870
Oh, that's an outlander.
噢，那是《古战场传奇》里的情节。

324
00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:14.410
Never mind.
算了，当我没说。

325
00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:16.170
That wasn't in.
那不是决斗规则里的。

326
00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:18.310
Jamie would bring Sassanac with him.
杰米会带着萨萨纳克一起去。

327
00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:19.290
Okay, never mind.
好吧，当我没说。

328
00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:19.610
Go.
继续。

329
00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:20.970
I don't know about that.
我不确定是不是这样。

330
00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:21.670
Okay.
好吧。

331
00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.810
I only read four to five websites.
我只看了四五个网站。

332
00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:24.910
Okay.
好吧。

333
00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.270
If we have a historian, perhaps they would know.
如果我们有位历史学家在场，或许他们会知道。

334
00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.810
You should watch Outlander, but don't watch it with your children around.
你应该看看《古战场传奇》，但别在孩子在场的时候看。

335
00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:31.370
Okay.
好吧。

336
00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:37.990
So listen, if a man felt like his honor had been insulted, he would tell his second to
听着，如果一个人觉得自己的尊严受到了侮辱，他会告诉他的代理人

337
00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.670
challenge the offender to a duel.
向冒犯者发起决斗挑战。

338
00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.150
You do not do it yourself.
你不能亲自去。

339
00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.250
You send your second.
你得派你的代理人去。

340
00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:48.790
The main duty of the second is to try to create a reconciliation, to avoid violence.
代理人的主要职责是尝试促成和解，以避免暴力。

341
00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:50.990
Oh, so that person's like the mediator.
噢，所以那个人就像调解员一样。

342
00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.770
Yeah, I mean, they're literally doing what all therapists tell us not to do,
是啊，我的意思是，他们实际上是在做所有心理咨询师告诉我们不要做的事，

343
00:15:54.910 --> 00:16:00.170
which is to triangulate communication in order to, you know, solve conflicts.
也就是通过三角沟通来解决冲突。

344
00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:01.770
But whatever, this is dueling.
但不管怎样，这就是决斗。

345
00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.610
I'm the second in my family.
我在家里就是那个“代理人”。

346
00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:07.650
I'm often the person sent in to smooth over the other stuff.
我经常是被派去平息各种矛盾的那个人。

347
00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:11.650
I think a lot of people have that position in their family.
我想很多人在家里都扮演着这个角色。

348
00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:12.310
I get it.
我懂。

349
00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:18.730
But if the second goes and said, hey, my guy is offended by you and wants to duel,
但如果代理人去了，说，嘿，我的人被你冒犯了，想要和你决斗，

350
00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:26.290
and the person says, great, we're dueling, the recipient of the duel challenge gets to pick
而对方说，好啊，我们决斗吧，那么接受决斗挑战的人有权选择

351
00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:30.190
the weapons and the time and the place of the duel.
决斗的武器、时间和地点。

352
00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:33.790
So, for example, James Shields,
比如，詹姆斯·希尔兹，

353
00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:39.730
an Illinois attorney general, challenged future president Abraham Lincoln to a duel.
一位伊利诺伊州的司法部长，曾向未来的总统亚伯拉罕·林肯发起决斗挑战。

354
00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.690
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

355
00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:47.770
Lincoln accepted the duel, and he chose the broadsword as their weapon.
林肯接受了决斗，并选择了宽刃剑作为武器。

356
00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.030
James Shields was like, what the F?
詹姆斯·希尔兹当时心想，这特么是什么鬼？

357
00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:52.530
That's insane.
这太疯狂了。

358
00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:53.990
Never mind.
算了。

359
00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:55.450
Forget it.
别提了。

360
00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.010
And he called off the duel.
于是他取消了决斗。

361
00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.970
So, like, bold move by Lincoln.
所以，林肯这一招真是大胆。

362
00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:04.590
Lincoln's like, I'll show up, and I'm bringing my sword to the duel.
林肯的态度是：我会准时赴约，而且我会带着我的剑去决斗。

363
00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:05.390
Do you want it?
你确定要来吗？

364
00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:08.110
Lincoln was like, I'm tall, and I'm a swordsman.
林肯当时的意思是：我个子高，而且我还是个剑客。

365
00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:08.730
Yeah.
没错。

366
00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.270
James Shields was like, never mind.
詹姆斯·希尔兹当时就想，还是算了吧。

367
00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.270
You know what?
你知道吗？

368
00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:12.570
I'm good.
我还是不去了。

369
00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:13.630
You know what?
你知道吗？

370
00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.750
I thought about it, and I'm okay.
我考虑了一下，我觉得还是算了。

371
00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.110
Here's one.
再讲一个。

372
00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.470
This one really got me.
这个真的惊到我了。

373
00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:22.630
I guess Andrew Jackson was very famous for dueling.
我听说安德鲁·杰克逊以好斗闻名。

374
00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:23.030
Oh.
哦。

375
00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.490
Lots of duels, this guy.
这家伙参加过很多次决斗。

376
00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:28.970
Experts placed his number of duels maybe as many as 100.
专家估计他参加的决斗次数可能多达100次。

377
00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:29.770
100.
100次。

378
00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.410
Was Andrew just pissing everyone off?
安德鲁当时是在到处惹人厌吗？

379
00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.590
He was just pissing everyone off.
他确实是在到处惹人厌。

380
00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:34.630
Everyone wanted to fight him.
每个人都想跟他打一架。

381
00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.630
His most famous duel was with Charles Dickinson.
他最著名的一场决斗是与查尔斯·迪金森进行的。

382
00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:41.230
not to be confused with Charles Dickens, the writer.
别和作家查尔斯·狄更斯搞混了。

383
00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.370
Oh, I was going to say, did you see my look on my face?
哦，我正想说呢，你看到我刚才的表情了吗？

384
00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.230
I was like, wait, wait, what?
我当时心想，等等，等等，什么？

385
00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.510
Yeah, no, Charles Dickinson, he was a horse breeder,
对，不是那个，查尔斯·迪金森，他是个养马人，

386
00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.290
and I guess these two guys hated each other.
我猜这两个人互相看不顺眼。

387
00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:54.710
Dickinson accused Jackson of cheating on a horse bet,
迪金森指责杰克逊在赌马中作弊，

388
00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.530
and he challenged Jackson to a duel.
于是他向杰克逊发起了决斗挑战。

389
00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.690
Jackson was like, I'll be there.
杰克逊回应说：我会准时赴约。

390
00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.390
The weapon is pistols.
武器是手枪。

391
00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:01.970
But here's the thing.
但重点来了。

392
00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:05.590
Dickinson was like known to be one of the best shots in the nation.
迪金森当时被公认为是全国枪法最好的人之一。

393
00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:10.270
So I don't know why Andrew Jackson picked pistols, but he did.
所以我不知道为什么安德鲁·杰克逊会选枪，但他确实选了。

394
00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:14.570
I think maybe it was just, I don't know, some swagger or something, right?
我觉得可能只是，我不知道，为了耍帅还是什么的，对吧？

395
00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.070
So they show up.
于是他们到了现场。

396
00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:17.130
They duel.
他们开始决斗。

397
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:17.870
Yeah.
没错。

398
00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.850
Dickinson got off the first shot.
迪金森先开了第一枪。

399
00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:22.650
It hit Andrew Jackson in the cheSt.
子弹击中了安德鲁·杰克逊的胸口。

400
00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.770
He's bleeding from the cheSt.
他胸口正在流血。

401
00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:25.190
Okay.
好吧。

402
00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:32.110
All accounts are that he, like, held one hand to the wound, lifted his pistol, fired at Dickinson.
据各方说法，他当时一只手按住伤口，举起手枪，向迪金森开火。

403
00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:33.770
His pistol misfired.
他的枪卡壳了。

404
00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:35.250
It didn't shoot.
没打响。

405
00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:35.790
Oh.
噢。

406
00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:40.910
So Andrew Jackson re-cocked his pistol, fired again, and killed Dickinson.
于是安德鲁·杰克逊重新扣动扳机，再次开火，打死了迪金森。

407
00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.990
This was very controversial, Angela.
安吉拉，这在当时非常有争议。

408
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:45.970
In the rules of dueling, you only get to fire once.
按照决斗规则，你只能开一枪。

409
00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.450
That's what I was going to say.
我正想说这个。

410
00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:48.430
Aren't you one and done?
不是说一枪定胜负吗？

411
00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:52.110
And I know nothing about dueling, but I was pretty sure that's the case.
我对决斗一窍不通，但我很确定是这样。

412
00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.110
Thank you, Hamilton.
谢谢你，汉密尔顿。

413
00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:54.490
That's right.
没错。

414
00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:55.990
Yeah.
是啊。

415
00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:57.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

416
00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:03.910
Andrew Jackson lived, he got away with it, and was later elected president of the United States.
安德鲁·杰克逊活了下来，他逃脱了惩罚，后来还当选为美国总统。

417
00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:05.170
I have a question.
我有个问题。

418
00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:05.910
What is it?
什么问题？

419
00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.050
If you're Charles Dickinson.
如果你是查尔斯·迪金森。

420
00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:08.530
Yep.
嗯。

421
00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.090
You see Andrew Jackson pointing his gun at you.
你看到安德鲁·杰克逊正用枪指着你。

422
00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:12.410
Right.
对。

423
00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:13.150
To fire.
准备开火。

424
00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.210
Do you run a zigzag?
你会跑Z字形吗？

425
00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:18.270
Can you step out of the way or do you just have to stand there?
你能躲开，还是只能站在那儿？

426
00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.170
Fingers crossed it doesn't hit you.
祈祷它打不中你？

427
00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.550
Is there no movement allowed?
是不允许移动吗？

428
00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:23.030
Can I not jump around?
我不能跳来跳去吗？

429
00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:24.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

430
00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:26.250
I don't know.
我不知道。

431
00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.610
Because I'm not going to stand in one place.
因为我可不会站在原地不动。

432
00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.150
If you're pointing a pistol at me, I'm going to get moving.
如果有人拿枪指着我，我肯定会跑起来。

433
00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.150
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.390
I think you're not allowed, Ange.
我觉得是不允许的，安吉。

435
00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:35.190
Oh.
噢。

436
00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:40.130
The last duel of record in the United States was in 1859.
美国有记录的最后一场决斗发生在1859年。

437
00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:41.250
Okay.
好吧。

438
00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:42.790
Here's who it involved.
参与者是这些人。

439
00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.190
Was it more white men shooting at each other?
又是白人男子互相射击吗？

440
00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.310
It sure was, lady.
没错，女士。

441
00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:52.270
Not only that, it was a United States senator and a retired chief justice of the California Supreme Court.
不仅如此，其中一位是美国参议员，另一位是加州最高法院的退休首席大法官。

442
00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:53.090
Oh.
噢。

443
00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:54.470
Way to go, guys.
真有你们的。

444
00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:54.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

445
00:19:55.110 --> 00:20:01.170
No one died in this duel because, listen to this madness, one guy's gun jammed.
这场决斗没人死亡，因为——听听这荒唐事——其中一人的枪卡壳了。

446
00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:01.710
Okay.
好吧。

447
00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:08.450
And then the other guy fired his gun, but it hit the other guy in his gold pocket watch, and they called a truce.
然后另一个人开了枪，但子弹打中了对方的金怀表，于是他们休战了。

448
00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:09.410
There you go.
这就对了。

449
00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.550
That was the last duel in America.
那就是美国最后一场决斗。

450
00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:12.650
All right.
好吧。

451
00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:18.510
Now, if Andrew Jackson was there, he would have unjammed his gun and shot at you again.
如果安德鲁·杰克逊当时在场，他肯定会修好枪再朝你开一枪。

452
00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:19.270
Right.
没错。

453
00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:20.210
Yeah.
是啊。

454
00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:26.090
I would like to say, I don't know who Andrew Jackson's second was, but I think they did a real shitty job.
我想说，我不知道安德鲁·杰克逊的助手是谁，但我认为他们工作做得真烂。

455
00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:27.850
What about Dickinson's second?
那迪金森的助手呢？

456
00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:36.630
And Dickinson's second tried to make a case that, you know, Andrew Jackson, I think, should be tried for murder, but no one wanted to hear about it.
迪金森的助手曾试图辩称，安德鲁·杰克逊应该因谋杀罪受审，但没人想听这些。

457
00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.170
That was very interesting.
那太有意思了。

458
00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.570
I liked all your dual trivia.
我很喜欢你说的所有关于决斗的冷知识。

459
00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:40.310
Thank you.
谢谢。

460
00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.890
I enjoyed researching my dual trivia.
我很享受研究这些决斗冷知识的过程。

461
00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:50.050
I mean, there is just a part of me that would do a history podcast with you, but we get everything slightly wrong.
我是说，我内心深处其实很想和你一起做个历史播客，尽管我们总会把事情搞错一点点。

462
00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:52.510
Well, we're already doing that.
好吧，我们已经在这么做了。

463
00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:57.690
I'm sure there are at least 12 things I did wrong in this fast fact number three.
我敢肯定，在刚才的第三个快讯里，我至少说错了12件事。

464
00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:58.710
You know what?
你知道吗？

465
00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.910
It's like our version of drunk history, but we're not drunk.
这就像是我们版的《醉酒史》，只不过我们没喝醉。

466
00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:02.670
Yes.
没错。

467
00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:07.710
We're just well-meaning ladies who Google and tell you history.
我们只是几个好心的女士，通过谷歌搜索来给大家讲讲历史。

468
00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:10.930
All right.
好吧。

469
00:21:11.110 --> 00:21:12.070
Should we take a break?
我们要休息一下吗？

470
00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.550
I think we should.
我觉得应该休息一下。

471
00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.350
There's a lot to say about this episode, and I can't wait.
